==Post-match==
[[File:Erik ten Hag 2017.jpg|thumb|upright=.8|[[Erik ten Hag]] became the first [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] manager to win trophies in successive seasons since [[Sir Alex Ferguson]]'s retirement, who last achieved that feat in [[2010–11 Manchester United F.C. season|2011]].]]

After the match, Erik ten Hag was questioned about his future, to which he replied: "I don't think about this. I'm in a project and we are exactly where we want to be."<ref name="SkySports2">{{cite news|last=Marsh|first=Charlotte|url=https://www.skysports.com/football/news/13865/13142901/man-utd-win-the-fa-cup-erik-ten-hag-says-he-will-go-somewhere-else-and-win-trophies-if-club-doesn-t-want-him|title=Man Utd win the FA Cup: Erik ten Hag says he will go somewhere else and win trophies if club doesn't want him|date=26 May 2024|access-date=26 May 2024|website=Sky Sports}}</ref> He also addressed criticism of him and his team this season: “We didn’t have the players. We (he and the critics) have seen the same things. There was not always good football, definitely not, but we had to make, all the time, compromises. Then you can’t play the football you want to play."<ref>{{cite web|last=Lee|first=Sam|url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5517688/2024/05/25/manchester-city-manchester-united-fa-cup/|title=Manchester City 1 Manchester United 2: A breathtaking team goal and Ten Hag gets it right to win FA Cup|date=26 May 2024|access-date=26 May 2024|website=The Athletic}}</ref> Pundit and former United midfielder Roy Keane suggested: "The manager has done his job today. Beating Man City in an FA Cup final is an extra bonus. Fingers crossed they support the manager."<ref name="SkySports2"/> Following weeks of speculation, reports emerged that Ten Hag would remain at United and that he was in talks with the club to sign a new deal. On 4 July, United announced that they had extended his contract until the 2025–26 season.<ref name="TenHagContractRenewal">{{cite news |url=https://www.manutd.com/en/news/detail/erik-ten-hag-extends-contract-as-manchester-united-manager |title=Ten Hag extends United contract |publisher=Manchester United |date=4 July 2024 |access-date=20 August 2024}}</ref> However, three months later, on 28 October, Ten Hag was sacked after a 2–1 defeat to [[West Ham United F.C.|West Ham United]] saw the club fall to 14th after nine games.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-10-28 |title=Erik ten Hag: Man Utd sack manager after defeat at West Ham |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cpvznn4v01yo |access-date=2025-01-06 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>

With his team's victory, Ten Hag became the first manager to beat [[Pep Guardiola]]'s Manchester City in a major domestic cup final.<ref>{{Cite web|date=25 May 2024|title=Man Utd stun Man City to win FA Cup|url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/4027998|access-date=27 May 2024|publisher=Premier League}}</ref> Having finished eighth in the [[2023–24 Premier League]], United also became the lowest ranked team to win the FA Cup since [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] under [[Mikel Arteta]] in [[2019–20 Arsenal F.C. season|2019–20]], when they also finished eighth. United goalscorer and [[Player of the match#Association football|man of the match]] Kobbie Mainoo praised the togetherness at the end of a tough season, adding his goal was "an amazing moment". He and teammate Alejandro Garnacho became the first teenagers to score in an FA Cup final since [[Cristiano Ronaldo]] for United in 2004. This was also City midfielder [[Rodri (footballer, born 1996)|Rodri]]'s first club defeat since February 2023 against Tottenham Hotspur, ending his 74-game unbeaten streak across all competitions.<ref name="Opta">{{cite news|url=https://theanalyst.com/eu/2024/05/manchester-city-vs-manchester-united-stats-fa-cup-final/|title=Manchester City 1-2 Manchester United Stats: Teenage Dreams for United As They Win FA Cup Final|date=25 May 2024|access-date=26 May 2024|publisher=[[Opta Sports]]|website=TheAnalyst.com}}</ref> City manager Guardiola commented that his game plan was not good: "The players know the reason why. Tactically it wasn't good. You plan for a game and different positions, but it didn't work."<ref name="SkySports2"/> 

As winners, United qualified for the [[2024–25 UEFA Europa League]] league phase and the [[2024 FA Community Shield]], where they faced City as the league champions.<ref name="SkySports"/> United earned £2{{nbsp}}million in prize money, runners-up City earned £1{{nbsp}}million.<ref name="FA KO TV money"/>

